<!-- Changes :
   o1_v03 : IDEA/ALLEGRO vertex detector described in FCC Feasibility Study Final Report (2025). An ultra-light inner vertex detector design with four layers is included as well, enabled by setting "nInnerVertexLayers" to 4, disabling the layers below "Vertex inner barrel" and instead enabling the ultra-light layers below "Ultra-light inner vertex"
   o1_v04 : Vertex disks have the better measurement direction now in phi (geometry unchanged). Reduced sensitive thickness for ultra-light curved vertex. Removed 'auxiliary pads' in the ultra-light curved vertex to increase the area that is sensitive by about 2.5% (see ALICE IT3 TDR). Ultra-light curved vertex detector sensors are now approximated by trapezoidal volumes, enabling the use of conformal tracking that currently requires non-bent surfaces.
            Refactored xml to such that each sub-component (inner barrel, outer barrel, disks, Kapton layer on beampipe, etc.) is a standalone xml file to make it easier in the future to mix and match e.g. different inner detector designs.
-->

<lccdd>
    <!--
        Complete, detailed vertex detector: Started with CLD vertex detector design from FCCDetectors, but adapted to describe IDEA engineered vertex detector design and extended functionality of detector builders
        Niloufar Alipour Tehrani (adapting original CLD version), Armin Ilg (adapting and extending to IDEA)
        A Vertex Detector for the FCC-ee IDEA detector concept, based on the engineered design by Fabrizio Palla and Filippo Bosi (INFN Pisa), implemented in DD4hep by Armin Ilg (UZH)
    -->

    <comment>Vertex inner barrel </comment>

    <define>
        <comment> To change to ultra-light inner vertex design, simply set nInnerVertexLayers to 4. Everything else is taken care of </comment>
        <constant name="nInnerVertexLayers" value="3"/>
    </define>

    <detectors>
        <comment> The envelope consists of a tube generally surrounding the vertex barrel and endcap disks, subtracted by a
            cone describing the upper acceptance of the LumiCal </comment>
        <detector name="Vertex" type="DD4hep_SubdetectorAssembly" vis="VXDVis">
            <type_flags type=" DetType_TRACKER + DetType_PIXEL + DetType_VERTEX"/>
            <shape type="BooleanShape" operation="Subtraction" material="Air">
                <shape type="BooleanShape" operation="Subtraction" material="Air">
                    <shape type="Tube" rmin="CentralBeamPipe_rmax+BeamPipeWidth" rmax="VTXOB_r_max_layer+VTXOB_rmax_clearance" dz="VTXD_z_max_total"/>
                    <shape type="Cone" rmin1="0" rmax1="tan(VertexClearanceTheta)*2000.0*mm" rmin2="0" rmax2="0" z="2000.0*mm/2."/>
                    <position x="0" y="0" z="-2000.0*mm/2." />
                </shape>                            
                <shape type="Cone" rmin1="0" rmax1="0" rmin2="0" rmax2="tan(VertexClearanceTheta)*2000.0*mm" z="2000.0*mm/2."/>
                <position x="0" y="0" z="2000.0*mm/2." />
            </shape>

            <comment>Vertex Assembly</comment>
            <composite name="VertexInnerBarrel"/>
            <composite name="Kapton_on_beampipe"/>
            <composite name="VertexInnerBarrel_tube"/>
            <comment>
                <composite name="VTXIB_Support_PEEK"/>
                <composite name="VTXIB_Support_CarbonFiber"/>
                <composite name="VTXIB_CoolingCones"/>
            </comment>
            <composite name="VertexOuterBarrel"/>
            <composite name="VertexDisks"/>
            <composite name="VertexDisks_support"/>
        </detector>
    </detectors>
    
    <comment> In the following there are three different options for the inner vertex detector, which can be selected by commenting out the other two options. The default is the IDEA inner vertex detector, which has an engineering design featured in the FCC Feasibility Study Report. </comment>

    <comment> Option 1: IDEA inner vertex detector based IDEA engineering design (INFN Pisa) using ARCADIA MAPS </comment>
    <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexInnerBarrel_o1_v04.xml"/>
    <define> <constant name="nInnerVertexLayers" value="3"/> </define>

    <comment> Option 2: Ultra-light inner vertex detector using ALICE ITS3-like stitched, curved MAPS </comment>
    <!-- <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexInnerBarrelUltraLight_o1_v04.xml"/> -->
    <!-- <define> <constant name="nInnerVertexLayers" value="4"/> </define> -->

    <comment> Option 3: FCC-SEED inner vertex detector using curved, overlapping MAPS </comment>
    <!-- <include ref="../../../ILD_FCCee/compact/ILD_common_FCCee/Vertex_FCC-SEED_barrel_o1_v01.xml"/>
    <define> <constant name="nInnerVertexLayers" value="5"/> </define> -->

    <comment> Vertex inner barrel support structure and cooling cones imported via DDCAD. Disabled because of overlaps within and with Vertex detector </comment>
    <!-- <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexInnerBarrel_CAD_supports_o1_v01.xml"/> -->

    <comment> Kapton layer on the beampipe, to separate the first vertex layer electrically from the beam pipe if the first layer is at r=11.8 mm </comment>
    <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/Vertex_kapton_on_beampipe_o1_v01.xml"/>

    <comment> Inner vertex outer tube, for keeping the air in for air cooling </comment>
    <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexInnerBarrel_support_tube_o1_v01.xml"/>

    <comment> IDEA outer vertex detector based on IDEA engineering design (INFN Pisa) using ATLASPix3 </comment>
    <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexOuterBarrel_o1_v04.xml"/>

    <comment> IDEA vertex disks based on IDEA engineering design (INFN Pisa) using ATLASPix3 </comment>
    <include ref="../../../IDEA/compact/IDEA_o1_v04/VertexDisks_o1_v04.xml"/>

    <readouts> <comment>  Definition of the readout segmentation/definition </comment>
        <readout name="VertexBarrelCollection"> 
            <segmentation type="MultiSegmentation" key="layer">
                <segmentation name="VTXIBgrid" type="CartesianGridXY" key_min="0" key_max="nInnerVertexLayers-1" grid_size_x="VTXIB_pitch_phi" grid_size_y="VTXIB_pitch_z"/> <comment> Segmentation for the ultra-light inner vertex </comment>
                <segmentation name="VTXOBgrid" type="CartesianGridXY" key_min="nInnerVertexLayers" key_max="nInnerVertexLayers+1" grid_size_x="VTXOB_pitch_phi" grid_size_y="VTXOB_pitch_z"/> <comment> Segmentation for the ultra-light inner vertex </comment>
            </segmentation>
            <id>${GlobalTrackerReadoutID},x:32:-16,y:-16</id>
        </readout>  
    </readouts>   

</lccdd>
